{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Loading bodies and joints in Delta Robot\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Identifying Directed Acyclic Graph, Spanning Tree and Chord Constraints\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The user-defined model is a list of bodies and joints. The input file specifies a Directed Graph (DG) with possible cycles. When the input file is loaded, the software identifies any user-specified joints that are not aligned with the spanning tree, and flips the sense as necessary, thereby converting the DG to a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) (i.e.\u160?with cycles removed). If any joints are identified to be not aligned with the spanning tree during this process, the user-defined sense of the inverse transformation is used across the joint to maintain the user-defined sign of the joint as specified in the input file. In the Delta robot model, all user-defined joints were specified to be aligned with the spanning tree and therefore it was not necessary to flip the sense of any joints.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 When the user input file is loaded, all user-defined bodies and joints are loaded into a {\f1 bodies} and {\f1 joints} list in the software. The pseudocode to identify the DAG and sort bodies and joints in level-increasing order follows below. The process starts by identifying all user specified joints with a connection to the fixed inertial reference frame as:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 @require joints\line
@return temp\line
@return joints\line
temp = []\line
for joint in joints:\line
  if joint.parent is fixed:\line
    joint.sense = positive\line
    joints.pop(joint)\line
    temp.append(joint)\line
  else if joint.child is fixed:\line
    joint.sense = negative\line
    joints.pop(joint)\line
    temp.append(joint)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If no joints with a connection to the fixed inertial reference frame are specified above, additional logic must be carried to reference a model to the fixed inertial reference frame using a 6DOF float joint. The additional logic for this operation is not discussed here.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After the above operation has been carried out, the temporary list {\f1 temp} will have been seeded with the first joints connected to the fixed frame. Bodies and joints are systematically removed from the user\u8217's initial list of bodies and joints specified in an arbitrary user-defined order in the input file and appended to the new temporary list of bodies and joints (specified as {\f1 bodies_temp} and {\f1 joints_temp} respectively below). In the below pseudocode, the notation {\f1 pop(0)} indicates to remove the first element of a list and {\f1 pop(element)} indicates to remove a specified element from the list. The notation {\f1 append(element)} indicates to append an element to the end of the list. The process continues sorting and flipping the sense of joints until all user-defined joints have been processed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 @require temp\line
@require bodies\line
@require joints\line
@return bodies\line
@return joints\line
@return chord_constraints\line
\line
bodies_temp = []\line
joints_temp = []\line
chord_constraints = []\line
\line
while(temp):\line
\line
  joint = temp.pop(0)\line
  joints_temp.append(joint)\line
\line
  if joint.sense is positive:\line
    body = joint.child\line
  else if joint.sense is negative:\line
    body = joint.parent\line
\line
  if body in bodies:\line
    bodies.pop(body)\line
    bodies_temp.append(body)\line
  else:\line
    virtualbody\line
    chordconstraint\line
    chordconstraint.parent = virtualbody\line
    if joint.sense is positive:\line
      chordconstraint.child = joint.child\line
      joint.child = virtualbody\line
    else if joint.sense is negative:\line
      chordconstraint.child = joint.parent\line
      joint.parent = virtualbody\line
    chord_constraints.append(chord_constraint)\line
    bodies_temp.append(virtualbody)\line
\line
  for joint in joints:\line
    if joint.parent is body:\line
      joint.sense = positive\line
      joints.pop(joint)\line
      temp.append(joint)\line
    else if joint.child is body:\line
      joint.sense = negative\line
      joints.pop(joint)\line
      temp.append(joint)\line
\line
bodies = bodies_temp\line
joints = joints_temp\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note that additional processing must be performed to identify and book-keep coordinate systems and shape matrices on bodies.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Delta Robot Model\par}
